% Transitive closure (transitive_closure.tcalc) in CHR notation.  Propagation
% rules read their heads.  CHR fires a propagation rule once per match by its
% propagation history; here the set store plays that part, since a firing
% that makes only rows already present is no step.
:- store(set).
edge(a, b). edge(b, c). edge(c, d).
base @ edge(X, Y) ==> path(X, Y).
step @ path(X, Y), edge(Y, Z) ==> path(X, Z).
